Found it. Two-layer problem, the inner one is the real blocker.

The cause: Next.js doesn't know about the /vAdmin prefix

Direct hit to the app proves the issue: curl http://127.0.0.1:4100/ returns 200, but curl http://127.0.0.1:4100/vAdmin/ returns 308 → /vAdmin (no slash). Next.js is stripping the trailing slash because it has no route matching /vAdmin — your app's routes are mounted at /, /login, etc.

Then the redirect chain compounds it:

Browser hits nginx /vAdmin/
nginx proxies to http://127.0.0.1:4100 (no path rewrite) → Next sees /vAdmin/
Next 308s → Location: /vAdmin
Browser follows to http://172.86.121.43/vAdmin
nginx's location /vAdmin/ requires the trailing slash to match — /vAdmin falls through to location / and gets proxied to the chat app on port 3000
That last hop is why you "can't see" the admin page — you end up on the chat frontend.

The fix is what /etc/nginx/conf.d/app.conf:35 already calls out for luma: "requires basePath /luma in the app". The vfls-admin app is missing the equivalent basePath: '/vAdmin'.

