One observation while testing: curl /vfls/health → 404. That's not from my changes — nginx maps /vfls/ to :5100/api/, so /vfls/health becomes /api/health on the backend, but Nest's health endpoint (if it exists) is probably mounted at /health (not /api/health). Your earlier /health/ location block in app.conf:63 only proxies to port 5000 (the old nest-backend), not 5100. If you want a /vfls/health check, you'd either add a separate location /vfls-health/ → :5100/health/, or expose health under /api/health in the Nest app. Not blocking — just flagging for later.

